🔥Offline First Investment App

🔸Functional requirements
- Display the user's portfolio and investment history.
- Show cached portfolio data when offline.
- Refresh data when the network becomes available.
- Allow users to initiate an investment when online.
- Show pending, successful, and failed transaction states.
- Keep portfolio data synchronized with the backend.
....................................................................................................

🔥Important scenarios to handle:

Scenario	                         Expected behavior
Internet unavailable	             Keep showing cached Room data; retry sync when appropriate.
API returns 401	                     Refresh authentication or request login; don't retry forever without valid credentials.
API returns 500/503	                 Retry with exponential backoff.
API returns invalid data	         Don't overwrite valid cached data.
App process is killed	             WorkManager can continue eligible work; observe its persisted status again when the app reopens.
User triggers sync repeatedly	     Use unique work to avoid duplicate sync jobs.
Two sync jobs run together	         Prevent stale responses from overwriting newer data.
Room insert fails	                 Roll back the transaction and retain the previous valid snapshot.
Sync is cancelled	                 Don't automatically display it as a network failure.
API succeeds but app crashes         before saving	A later sync should safely fetch and save the data again.
offline write                        set status pending and trigger update request from worker if status pending in

